  "contracts": [
    "Existing crt_numeric_bits C/header are adopted byte-for-byte. Prior6 pinned Ghidra records cover the solved algorithms; no unchanged algorithm is rewritten or retested. Fifteen Native mappings remain on those exact bodies;3 logical functions remain shared C helpers without duplicate Native credit.",
    "00567575 actual Native MOV EDX/AND/OR leaves EAX and ECX untouched. C normalized scalar represents full EDX, never a replacement classification. Parent must retain its actual EAX classification; Native562D1D immediately CMPs EAX after the call. No invented incoming flag/register frame is introduced.",
    "Shared slot is4 bytes with two WORDs at0/2. Normalizer reads only original low WORD, writes upper WORD and executes FLDCW from that shared upper WORD. Parent retains actual initial upper bits when normalization is skipped; no zeroed scratch assumption is made. Size/offset are statically asserted.",
    "00568532 performs real waiting FSTSW and reuses solved signed-WORD conversion. Full EAX is sign extension;567F58 consumes actual low exception bits. Hardware status is not an external fabricated input anymore.",
    "0056854F performs waiting FSTCW, reuses solved low-WORD mask computation and always FLDCW, including mask0. Original control is returned sign-extended. Native high scratch bits from incoming ECX do not affect the loaded WORD or EAX; sole direct56971F caller pops both args, and its next matherr/error callees do not consume incoming ECX. No unobserved high-stack-garbage input is invented. Indirect/full-register equivalence remains unclaimed.",
    "Compiled object confirms waiting status/control reads, partial WORD store at slot+2, control loads and real calls to the3 existing C logical helpers. All27 public symbols across the two units occur once; previous6 live x87 bodies are byte-identical.",
    "Unchanged 96-bit arithmetic, raw IEEE conversion, formatting bindings, unsigned64 operations and flags/control conversion retain their prior Native-derived input/producer domains. This checkpoint does not broaden exceptional/malformed input or machine-register coverage."
  ],
